{
  "$comment": [
    "THE DESIGN-QUERY EVAL CORPUS.",
    "",
    "Each task states a request a person would type into the 'describe the",
    "report in words' row over the sales-star fixture model",
    "(tests/fixtures/model/sales_star.json + sales_star_strategy.json), the",
    "query that answers it, and a `distractor`: the plausible wrong query a",
    "model reaches for, which MUST NOT be equal to the reference. A task whose",
    "distractor equals its reference measures nothing and is a defect.",
    "",
    "Layer A (CI, no model): every reference parses and compiles against the",
    "fixture with no errors; every distractor differs from its reference in",
    "canonical form; every name a reference uses is among the candidates the",
    "assistant would show a model for that intent.",
    "",
    "Equality is CANONICAL (canonical.ts): names case-insensitive, layout",
    "directives unordered, SORT and TOP N included.",
    "",
    "SORT orders row and column LABELS only; the DSL ranks by a measure's",
    "value solely through TOP/BOTTOM N BY [Measure]. Every 'highest first'",
    "task therefore expects TOP N, never SORT: [Measure].",
    "",
    "Filter values are plausible member names; the fixture carries no rows, so",
    "they are not verified against data. Subcategory is snowflaked and is left",
    "out of the references: the query engine refuses paths longer than one hop.",
    "",
    "A task may list `alternatives`: other queries that answer the request",
    "equally well (Date.Month vs Date.MonthName; the Swedish \"marginal\" that is",
    "either margin measure). Layer A requires each to compile, to differ from",
    "the reference and from the distractor; Layer B grades any of them as a pass."
  ],
  "version": 1,
